{
  "part": 1,
  "total_clips": 25,
  "clips": [
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_01",
      "chapter": "[COLD OPEN]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_01.mp3",
      "duration_s": 18.851,
      "words": 43,
      "wpm": 136.9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 0,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "About three thousand two hundred years ago, a walled city on a windy hill in what is now Turkey burned to the ground. What came after is a mix of poetry, memory, and shovel work. The Greeks said it fell over one woman.",
          "words": 43,
          "t_start": 0.33,
          "t_end": 18.301,
          "duration_s": 17.971
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_02",
      "chapter": "[COLD OPEN]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_02.mp3",
      "duration_s": 18.986,
      "words": 39,
      "wpm": 123.2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 0,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "Their poets blamed a grudge between goddesses. Archaeologists point to something far less romantic. So which one is it? To find out, we start where the Greeks started: with a wedding, and a guest list that went very wrong.",
          "words": 39,
          "t_start": 0.12,
          "t_end": 18.786,
          "duration_s": 18.666
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_03",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 1: THE UNINVITED GUEST]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_03.mp3",
      "duration_s": 12.707,
      "words": 28,
      "wpm": 132.2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 1,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "The groom was a mortal king named Peleus. The bride was Thetis, a sea goddess so lovely that Zeus himself had wanted her, until he heard a prophecy.",
          "words": 28,
          "t_start": 0.323,
          "t_end": 12.169,
          "duration_s": 11.846
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_04",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 1: THE UNINVITED GUEST]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_04.mp3",
      "duration_s": 14.657,
      "words": 32,
      "wpm": 131.0,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 1,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "Her son, it said, would grow up greater than his father. Suddenly no god wanted anything to do with her. Marry her to a mortal, they decided, and the problem goes away.",
          "words": 32,
          "t_start": 0.167,
          "t_end": 14.378,
          "duration_s": 14.211
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_05",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 1: THE UNINVITED GUEST]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_05.mp3",
      "duration_s": 19.278,
      "words": 42,
      "wpm": 130.7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 2,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "So Olympus came to the wedding. Music, wine, mountains of food. And one missing guest. Eris, the goddess of strife, had not been invited.",
          "words": 24,
          "t_start": 0.16,
          "t_end": 9.772,
          "duration_s": 9.612
        },
        {
          "line_index": 3,
          "speaker": "MASCOT",
          "voice_id": "voice-01",
          "text": "Spoiler. Terrible idea.",
          "words": 3,
          "t_start": 10.039,
          "t_end": 12.13,
          "duration_s": 2.091
        },
        {
          "line_index": 4,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "She showed up anyway.",
          "words": 4,
          "t_start": 12.397,
          "t_end": 13.884,
          "duration_s": 1.487
        },
        {
          "line_index": 5,
          "speaker": "ERIS",
          "voice_id": "voice-04",
          "text": "Don't mind me. I only came to drop off a gift.",
          "words": 11,
          "t_start": 14.151,
          "t_end": 19.011,
          "duration_s": 4.86
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_06",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 1: THE UNINVITED GUEST]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_06.mp3",
      "duration_s": 18.319,
      "words": 40,
      "wpm": 131.0,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 6,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "She rolled a golden apple across the floor. Scratched into it were the words: for the most beautiful.",
          "words": 18,
          "t_start": 0.213,
          "t_end": 8.452,
          "duration_s": 8.239
        },
        {
          "line_index": 7,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "Three goddesses reached for it at once.",
          "words": 7,
          "t_start": 8.807,
          "t_end": 10.786,
          "duration_s": 1.978
        },
        {
          "line_index": 8,
          "speaker": "HERA",
          "voice_id": "voice-04",
          "text": "Obviously it's mine. I'm the queen of heaven.",
          "words": 8,
          "t_start": 11.141,
          "t_end": 14.658,
          "duration_s": 3.517
        },
        {
          "line_index": 9,
          "speaker": "ATHENA",
          "voice_id": "voice-04",
          "text": "Beauty fades. Wisdom doesn't. Hand it over.",
          "words": 7,
          "t_start": 15.013,
          "t_end": 17.964,
          "duration_s": 2.951
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_07",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 1: THE UNINVITED GUEST]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_07.mp3",
      "duration_s": 14.639,
      "words": 32,
      "wpm": 131.2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 10,
          "speaker": "APHRODITE",
          "voice_id": "voice-04",
          "text": "Please. I'm the goddess of beauty. It practically has my name on it.",
          "words": 13,
          "t_start": 0.196,
          "t_end": 5.957,
          "duration_s": 5.761
        },
        {
          "line_index": 11,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "They turned to Zeus, and Zeus, who had not stayed king by being foolish, wanted no part of it.",
          "words": 19,
          "t_start": 6.283,
          "t_end": 14.313,
          "duration_s": 8.03
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_08",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 1: THE UNINVITED GUEST]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_08.mp3",
      "duration_s": 16.44,
      "words": 36,
      "wpm": 131.4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 12,
          "speaker": "ZEUS",
          "voice_id": "voice-03",
          "text": "Pick one of you, and I make two enemies. Not a chance. Find a mortal.",
          "words": 15,
          "t_start": 0.264,
          "t_end": 6.002,
          "duration_s": 5.738
        },
        {
          "line_index": 13,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "Far away on Mount Ida, a young shepherd named Paris was minding his flock. He was secretly a prince of Troy.",
          "words": 21,
          "t_start": 6.441,
          "t_end": 16.001,
          "duration_s": 9.56
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_09",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 1: THE UNINVITED GUEST]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_09.mp3",
      "duration_s": 18.795,
      "words": 41,
      "wpm": 130.9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 13,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "At his birth, his mother had dreamed her baby would set the city on fire, so the king ordered him left on a mountainside. Troy had tried to avoid its own destruction, and ended up raising its destroyer in a hut.",
          "words": 41,
          "t_start": 0.192,
          "t_end": 18.474,
          "duration_s": 18.282
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_10",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 1: THE UNINVITED GUEST]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_10.mp3",
      "duration_s": 19.258,
      "words": 42,
      "wpm": 130.9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 14,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "Each goddess came to him alone, with an offer.",
          "words": 9,
          "t_start": 0.189,
          "t_end": 3.946,
          "duration_s": 3.757
        },
        {
          "line_index": 15,
          "speaker": "HERA",
          "voice_id": "voice-04",
          "text": "Choose me, and you rule every kingdom between here and the sunrise.",
          "words": 12,
          "t_start": 4.261,
          "t_end": 9.409,
          "duration_s": 5.147
        },
        {
          "line_index": 16,
          "speaker": "ATHENA",
          "voice_id": "voice-04",
          "text": "Choose me, and no one will ever beat you in battle.",
          "words": 11,
          "t_start": 9.724,
          "t_end": 14.385,
          "duration_s": 4.661
        },
        {
          "line_index": 17,
          "speaker": "APHRODITE",
          "voice_id": "voice-04",
          "text": "Choose me, and the most beautiful woman alive is yours.",
          "words": 10,
          "t_start": 14.7,
          "t_end": 18.943,
          "duration_s": 4.243
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_11",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 1: THE UNINVITED GUEST]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_11.mp3",
      "duration_s": 10.666,
      "words": 21,
      "wpm": 118.1,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 18,
          "speaker": "PARIS",
          "voice_id": "voice-02",
          "text": "Sorry, Hera. Sorry, Athena.",
          "words": 4,
          "t_start": 0.12,
          "t_end": 2.808,
          "duration_s": 2.688
        },
        {
          "line_index": 19,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "Aphrodite got the apple. The most beautiful woman alive was named Helen. And Helen was already married.",
          "words": 17,
          "t_start": 3.008,
          "t_end": 10.466,
          "duration_s": 7.458
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_12",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 2: THE OATH]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_12.mp3",
      "duration_s": 17.188,
      "words": 38,
      "wpm": 132.7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 20,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "Helen was the daughter of Tyndareus, king of Sparta, and when she came of age, nearly every important man in Greece arrived to ask for her hand. Tyndareus panicked.",
          "words": 29,
          "t_start": 0.33,
          "t_end": 12.321,
          "duration_s": 11.991
        },
        {
          "line_index": 21,
          "speaker": "TYNDAREUS",
          "voice_id": "voice-03",
          "text": "Whoever I choose, the rest will tear Greece apart.",
          "words": 9,
          "t_start": 12.871,
          "t_end": 16.638,
          "duration_s": 3.767
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_13",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 2: THE OATH]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_13.mp3",
      "duration_s": 16.252,
      "words": 35,
      "wpm": 129.2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 22,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "The man who solved it was Odysseus, who had no real chance at Helen himself.",
          "words": 15,
          "t_start": 0.12,
          "t_end": 6.612,
          "duration_s": 6.492
        },
        {
          "line_index": 23,
          "speaker": "ODYSSEUS",
          "voice_id": "voice-02",
          "text": "Then make them swear first. Whoever wins, every other suitor defends his marriage. And in return, help me win Penelope.",
          "words": 20,
          "t_start": 6.812,
          "t_end": 16.052,
          "duration_s": 9.24
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_14",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 2: THE OATH]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_14.mp3",
      "duration_s": 17.439,
      "words": 38,
      "wpm": 130.7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 24,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "Tyndareus sacrificed a horse, and the suitors swore standing over its remains.",
          "words": 12,
          "t_start": 0.148,
          "t_end": 5.604,
          "duration_s": 5.456
        },
        {
          "line_index": 25,
          "speaker": "MASCOT",
          "voice_id": "voice-01",
          "text": "Keep that horse in mind.",
          "words": 5,
          "t_start": 5.852,
          "t_end": 7.729,
          "duration_s": 1.877
        },
        {
          "line_index": 26,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "Helen chose Menelaus, a king with a famous brother. That brother was Agamemnon of Mycenae, the most powerful ruler in Greece.",
          "words": 21,
          "t_start": 7.976,
          "t_end": 17.192,
          "duration_s": 9.216
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_15",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 2: THE OATH]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_15.mp3",
      "duration_s": 14.165,
      "words": 31,
      "wpm": 131.3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 27,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "Years later, Paris arrived in Sparta as a guest. Menelaus was called away to Crete, and when he came home, his wife and a good part of his treasure were gone.",
          "words": 31,
          "t_start": 0.212,
          "t_end": 13.811,
          "duration_s": 13.599
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_16",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 2: THE OATH]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_16.mp3",
      "duration_s": 16.222,
      "words": 38,
      "wpm": 140.5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 27,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "Did Helen leave willingly, or was she taken? The Greeks never agreed. In Homer, Helen blames herself bitterly for the rest of her life.",
          "words": 24,
          "t_start": 0.33,
          "t_end": 9.774,
          "duration_s": 9.444
        },
        {
          "line_index": 28,
          "speaker": "MENELAUS",
          "voice_id": "voice-03",
          "text": "He sat at my table. He ate my food. And he took my wife.",
          "words": 14,
          "t_start": 10.324,
          "t_end": 15.672,
          "duration_s": 5.348
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_17",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 2: THE OATH]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_17.mp3",
      "duration_s": 11.324,
      "words": 25,
      "wpm": 132.5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 29,
          "speaker": "AGAMEMNON",
          "voice_id": "voice-03",
          "text": "Then we call in the oath. Every king who ever courted Helen sails with us.",
          "words": 15,
          "t_start": 0.321,
          "t_end": 6.805,
          "duration_s": 6.484
        },
        {
          "line_index": 30,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "Except that some of them did not want to go.",
          "words": 10,
          "t_start": 7.34,
          "t_end": 10.789,
          "duration_s": 3.45
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_18",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 3: THE FLEET AT AULIS]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_18.mp3",
      "duration_s": 18.8,
      "words": 41,
      "wpm": 130.9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 31,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "Odysseus, king of Ithaca, had a new baby and a happy home. When the recruiters arrived, he pretended to be out of his mind. He yoked a donkey and an ox to a plow and began sowing the beach with salt.",
          "words": 41,
          "t_start": 0.184,
          "t_end": 18.493,
          "duration_s": 18.309
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_19",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 3: THE FLEET AT AULIS]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_19.mp3",
      "duration_s": 17.526,
      "words": 33,
      "wpm": 113.0,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 32,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "A man named Palamedes saw through it. He laid Odysseus's infant son in front of the plow.",
          "words": 17,
          "t_start": 0.12,
          "t_end": 8.153,
          "duration_s": 8.034
        },
        {
          "line_index": 33,
          "speaker": "PALAMEDES",
          "voice_id": "voice-03",
          "text": "Keep plowing, my king. Straight ahead.",
          "words": 6,
          "t_start": 8.353,
          "t_end": 10.727,
          "duration_s": 2.373
        },
        {
          "line_index": 34,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "Odysseus swerved.",
          "words": 2,
          "t_start": 10.927,
          "t_end": 12.538,
          "duration_s": 1.611
        },
        {
          "line_index": 35,
          "speaker": "ODYSSEUS",
          "voice_id": "voice-02",
          "text": "All right. You made your point. I'll go.",
          "words": 8,
          "t_start": 12.738,
          "t_end": 17.326,
          "duration_s": 4.588
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_20",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 3: THE FLEET AT AULIS]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_20.mp3",
      "duration_s": 10.987,
      "words": 24,
      "wpm": 131.1,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 36,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "He never forgave Palamedes, which, as we will see, ended badly for Palamedes.",
          "words": 13,
          "t_start": 0.136,
          "t_end": 5.709,
          "duration_s": 5.573
        },
        {
          "line_index": 37,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "The Greeks also needed Achilles, the best warrior of his generation.",
          "words": 11,
          "t_start": 5.936,
          "t_end": 10.76,
          "duration_s": 4.825
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_21",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 3: THE FLEET AT AULIS]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_21.mp3",
      "duration_s": 15.965,
      "words": 37,
      "wpm": 139.1,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 37,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "His mother Thetis knew he was fated to die at Troy, so she hid him among the daughters of a king on the island of Skyros, where he fell in love and fathered a son named Neoptolemus.",
          "words": 37,
          "t_start": 0.33,
          "t_end": 15.415,
          "duration_s": 15.085
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_22",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 3: THE FLEET AT AULIS]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_22.mp3",
      "duration_s": 15.555,
      "words": 34,
      "wpm": 131.1,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 38,
          "speaker": "THETIS",
          "voice_id": "voice-04",
          "text": "Stay hidden, my son. If you go to Troy, you will not come home.",
          "words": 14,
          "t_start": 0.206,
          "t_end": 6.09,
          "duration_s": 5.884
        },
        {
          "line_index": 39,
          "speaker": "ACHILLES",
          "voice_id": "voice-02",
          "text": "A long life that nobody remembers, or a short one that nobody forgets. It's not much of a choice, Mother.",
          "words": 20,
          "t_start": 6.433,
          "t_end": 15.211,
          "duration_s": 8.777
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_23",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 3: THE FLEET AT AULIS]",
      "file_path": "production/part1/vo/p1_clip_23.mp3",
      "duration_s": 17.89,
      "words": 39,
      "wpm": 130.8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "line_index": 40,
          "speaker": "NARRATOR",
          "voice_id": "voice-00",
          "text": "The fleet gathered at a harbor called Aulis, and then it sat there. No wind. Day after day, the sails hung limp.",
          "words": 22,
          "t_start": 0.166,
          "t_end": 9.869,
          "duration_s": 9.703
        },
        {
          "line_index": 41,
          "speaker": "CALCHAS",
          "voice_id": "voice-03",
          "text": "Artemis is angry. The wind returns when your daughter Iphigenia is sacrificed.",
          "words": 12,
          "t_start": 10.146,
          "t_end": 15.301,
          "duration_s": 5.155
        },
        {
          "line_index": 42,
          "speaker": "AGAMEMNON",
          "voice_id": "voice-03",
          "text": "Not her. Anyone but her.",
          "words": 5,
          "t_start": 15.577,
          "t_end": 17.614,
          "duration_s": 2.036
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "clip_id": "p1_clip_24",
      "chapter": "[CHAPTER 3: THE FLEET AT AULIS]",
